%% Edge Optimizer - current architecture and architectural flaws
%%
%% Evidence basis: static code inspection on 2026-09-28 against architecture.md
%% and the blueprints/ contracts. No build, service, named-pipe, or GUI behavior
%% was exercised to produce this diagram.
%%
%% Reading guide
%%   Solid arrows      : implemented runtime paths (transport noted on the edge)
%%   Dotted arrows     : attack or failure paths that the current code permits
%%   Fx nodes          : architectural flaws, linked to the component they affect
%%   Colors            : red = Critical, orange = High, yellow = Medium
%%
%% Flaw index (file references are the primary evidence)
%%   F1  Engine pipe uses a NULL security descriptor, a machine-global name, no
%%       FILE_FLAG_FIRST_PIPE_INSTANCE and no PIPE_REJECT_REMOTE_CLIENTS
%%       (crates/core/src/engine_ipc.rs:9, 22-31). Runner connects without
%%       verifying the server process (crates/runner/src/main.rs:592-612).
%%   F2  Engine never authenticates its client: no client PID, image, or SID
%%       check before SYSTEM-level process termination
%%       (crates/engine_service/src/main.rs:24-48).
%%   F3  Runner accepts any same-user client on the Settings pipe and persists or
%%       acts on its messages (crates/core/src/ipc.rs:144-168,
%%       crates/runner/src/main.rs handle_settings_message).
%%   F4  Macro worker accepts any same-user client and applies its configuration,
%%       which drives synthetic input (crates/macro/src/ipc_handler.rs:49-126).
%%   F5  The privileged engine is a console loop registered as a SYSTEM scheduled
%%       task, not an SCM service; the installer defaults to a user-writable
%%       target\release binary (scripts/install-engine-service.ps1:2-11).
%%   F6  One malformed or failed read ends the engine: recv errors propagate with
%%       `?` out of main, and the scheduled task has no recovery action
%%       (crates/engine_service/src/main.rs:30-31).
%%   F7  Termination targets are raw name strings; the full Profile is sent to the
%%       SYSTEM process; Runner does not pre-validate; matching is name-only with
%%       no PID re-check (TOCTOU) and a 10-entry blocklist
%%       (crates/core/src/orchestration.rs:185-189, crates/core/src/process.rs:35-114).
%%   F8  Runner performs blocking engine IPC (5 s ping, up to 2 s connect timeout)
%%       and full process enumeration on its tray message-pump thread
%%       (crates/runner/src/main.rs:251-266, 386-394, 592-612).
%%   F9  Workers are not placed in a Job object; they are only killed on Drop, so
%%       a crashed Runner leaves orphaned overlay and input-injecting workers
%%       (crates/core/src/crosshair_overlay.rs, crates/core/src/macro_worker.rs).
%%   F10 Protocol versioning is incomplete: GuiToTray and RunnerToMacroCommand
%%       carry no version, and Runner and the engine never check
%%       Envelope.protocol_version (crates/core/src/ipc.rs:34-82, 251-256).
%%   F11 The C# client hand-writes a Bincode codec that mirrors Rust structs with
%%       no shared schema; Runner never calls Profile::validate or macro
%%       validation before persisting
%%       (TransitionalBincodeRunnerClient.cs:270-421, crates/core/src/profile.rs:27-57).
%%   F12 The crosshair worker's contract is CLI arguments with an arbitrary image
%%       path, no dimension or size limit before decode, and no Runner channel;
%%       validate_crosshair_image is never called at runtime
%%       (crates/crosshair/src/main.rs:10-36, crates/core/src/image_picker.rs:7).
%%   F13 Macro playback runs synchronously on the hotkey loop with no
%%       cancellation, unbounded repeat counts, UntilKeyPressed executing once, and
%%       Shutdown calling process::exit without releasing held input
%%       (crates/macro/src/executor.rs:35-96, crates/macro/src/ipc_handler.rs:132-134).
%%   F14 IdempotencyCache is an unbounded HashSet of client-controlled request IDs
%%       in both Runner and the engine (crates/core/src/orchestration.rs:212-220).
%%   F15 Legacy JSON persistence (GamingOptimizer under APPDATA) is still compiled
%%       and its load errors collapse to defaults during import
%%       (crates/core/src/config.rs:48-78, crates/runner/src/main.rs:118-122).
%%   F16 The core crate mixes domain and protocol code with Win32 presentation:
%%       the deprecated flyout.rs (762 lines), tray_icon, an unused low-level
%%       keyboard hook (input_recorder.rs), and image_picker (crates/core/src/lib.rs).
%%   F17 crates/runner/src/main.rs combines the tray pump, Settings IPC server,
%%       orchestration, engine client, legacy import, and worker lifecycle on one
%%       thread in one file.
%%   F18 The Settings client seeds hard-coded profiles before Runner hydration,
%%       violating the presentation-only, no-mock-data rule
%%       (MainWindowViewModel.cs:45-48).
%%   F19 Three divergent key-mapping tables (hotkey registration, playback, and
%%       recording) allow shortcuts that register but cannot be played back
%%       (crates/macro/src/hotkey_manager.rs, crates/macro/src/executor.rs,
%%       crates/core/src/input_recorder.rs).

